# WEKA Storage

WEKA provides the shared high-performance storage layer for the environment. Linux clients can mount storage through either the native WEKA filesystem client or NFS v4. Control-plane nodes and compute trays reach storage through their storage interfaces.

Use the storage interfaces on the control-plane nodes and compute trays when connecting to WEKA. Treat this as a storage data path, separate from north-south host routing, management addresses, BMC addresses, and east-west compute fabric traffic.

## Storage Access

| Method | Mount Target | Access Path |
|---|---|---|
| Native WEKA client | `{{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_backends | join(',') }}/{{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_filesystem }}` | Use the storage interface created on the client host. |
| NFS v4 | `{{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_hostname }}:{{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_export }}` (`{{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_range }}`) | Use the storage interface path. |

## Native WEKA Client

Install the WEKA client from the storage service, create the mount point, and specify the storage interface or bond you created with `-o net=...`. Use the core list for the type of system you are mounting from.

```bash
curl http://{{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_hostname }}:14000/dist/v1/install | WEKA_CGROUPS_MODE=force_v2 sh

mkdir -p {{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_mount_path }}
```

### Compute Trays

```bash
mount -t wekafs \
  -o core={{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_compute_tray_cores | join(',') }} \
  -o net={{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_net_interface }} \
  {{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_backends | join(',') }}/{{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_filesystem }} \
  {{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_mount_path }}
```

### Control-Plane Nodes

```bash
mount -t wekafs \
  -o core={{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_control_plane_cores | join(',') }} \
  -o net={{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_net_interface }} \
  {{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_backends | join(',') }}/{{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_filesystem }} \
  {{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_mount_path }}
```

In the examples above, `{{ gb300nvl72_weka_client_net_interface }}` is the storage interface. Replace it with the interface or bond name created on your client if your configuration uses a different name.

## NFS v4

NFS mounts should use the `{{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_hostname }}` host record, which resolves to the storage service IPs in `{{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_range }}`. Do not mount through WEKA management or BMC addresses.

```bash
mkdir -p {{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_mount_path }}

mount -t nfs {{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_hostname }}:{{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_export }} {{ gb300nvl72_weka_nfs_mount_path }}
```

## Client Software

Use only the native WEKA client or the NFS v4 mount path documented above. SMB access is not enabled for this environment.

